# Paths excluded from the Cloudflare Workers static-assets upload.
#
# wrangler deploy scans the assets directory (here, the repo root) and rejects
# any single file > 25 MiB. When Cloudflare clones the repo it can create a Git
# pack file > 25 MiB inside .git/objects/pack/ (the large media lives in
# history), which fails the build with "Asset too large" even though no served
# file is that big. See cloudflare/workerd#4336.
#
# Patterns use .gitignore syntax. We exclude .git every way it can match AND the
# pack files by extension (belt-and-suspenders — the extension rules guarantee
# the oversized pack is dropped regardless of directory-match edge cases).

# --- Git internals (the actual cause of the error) ---
.git
.git/
**/.git
**/.git/
**/.git/**
*.pack
*.idx
*.rev
*.bitmap

# --- Wrangler / tooling files (not part of the site) ---
.wrangler
.wrangler/
**/.wrangler/**
.gitignore
.assetsignore
wrangler.jsonc
wrangler.toml
node_modules
node_modules/
**/node_modules/**

# --- Editor / OS cruft ---
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# --- Internal docs — not served to users ---
*.md

# --- Archived originals kept for reversibility, but not served (saves ~35 MB) ---
assets/_archive
